# Product Modularization

**Production config:** stored on **`tenants`** row — `edition`, `modules`, `roles_enabled`, `dashboard_layout`, **`locale`** (`zh-TW` \| `en`).

**Presets:** `deploy/presets/personal.yaml`, `professional.yaml` — applied at tenant onboarding. **`deploy/config.yaml`** — local dev / single-tenant bootstrap only until tenant-backed config ships.

**Backend:**

```text
core/deployment.py, capabilities.py, db.py (SQLAlchemy)
core/tenant.py (resolution, current tenant context)
alembic/
modules/{inventory,orders,analytics}/
repositories/postgres/   # tenant-scoped
schemas/, models/
```

`main.py`: **register all module routers**; enforce modules per request via capabilities → `module_disabled` (ADR 005). Do **not** omit routers at startup based on global YAML.

`GET /api/deployment` → current tenant's modules, capabilities, **locale**, `dashboard_layout`.

**Frontend:** i18n (`react-i18next`). Always show a language control (`zh-TW` \| `en`) in the header or settings — user can switch at any time. Prefer the saved user choice; if none, fall back to tenant `locale` from `GET /api/deployment`, then `en`. Language is **not** a module and is **not** locked at signup.

**Repositories:** `StockRepository`, `OrderRepository`; tenant-scoped queries; services never use raw SQL in routes.

**Avoid:** `MONGO_URI`; `staff` / `guest` roles; UI-only module hides; non-stock inventory schemas; global single-owner signup gate.
